Key details: rising edges of request signals. Need retention of previous states. Also recipeQueryResult retains last successful query until another successful query — so don't clear on idle.

error/status clear on idle — but what about on non-idle successful op? On success, error=false, status=0. Also success pulses: recipeAdded etc. should be cleared each call and set true only on successful op.

Implement:

```
IF addRecipe AND NOT rtAdd THEN
   ... handle
ELSIF deleteRecipe AND NOT rtDel THEN
...
```
Actually requests use rising edges; at most one rises per call. Simple.

Detect duplicate: loop over recipe array, if recipe[i].recipeID = recipeIn.recipeID AND recipeIn.recipeID <> 0.

Add: 
- duplicate -> error true, status 16#8002
- else find empty slot (recipeID=0) -> if none, status 16#8003
- else insert.

Delete: find index with ID; if not found -> 16#8004; else recipe[i].recipeID := 0.

Modify: find; if not found -> 16#8005; else recipe[i] := recipeIn.

Query: find; if not found -> 16#8001; else recipeQueryResult := recipe[i].

Write code.

```
// reset pulses
recipeAdded := FALSE;
recipeDeleted := FALSE;
recipeModified := FALSE;
error := FALSE;
status := 0;

foundIndex := 0;
FOR i := 1 TO 10 DO
    IF recipe[i].recipeID = recipeIn.recipeID AND recipeIn.recipeID <> 0 THEN
        foundIndex := i;
        EXIT;
    END_IF
END_FOR
```
Wait careful: duplicate check needs its own flag. But foundIndex is enough: if foundIndex>0, ID exists.

Now handle each request.

Query:
```
IF queryRecipe AND NOT rtQuery THEN
    IF foundIndex = 0 THEN
        error := TRUE; status := 16#8001;
    ELSE
        recipeQueryResult := recipe[foundIndex];
    END_IF
END_IF
```

Add:
```
IF addRecipe AND NOT rtAdd THEN
    IF foundIndex <> 0 THEN
        error := TRUE; status := 16#8002;
    ELSE
        emptyIndex := 0;
        FOR i := 1 TO 10 DO
            IF recipe[i].recipeID = 0 THEN
                emptyIndex := i;
                EXIT;
            END_IF
        END_FOR
        IF emptyIndex = 0 THEN
            error := TRUE; status := 16#8003;
        ELSE
            recipe[emptyIndex] := recipeIn;
            recipeAdded := TRUE;
        END_IF
    END_IF
END_IF
```

Delete / modify similar.

Then update edge memories:
rtAdd := addRecipe; etc.

One consideration: when error occurs, error := TRUE and status set; else error false status 0. Good. What if recipeIn.recipeID = 0 with add? Assumption says only positive nonzero IDs. Handle: if recipeIn.recipeID = 0 for add, all slots look empty... hmm, duplicate check with 0 skips. Insertion into first empty slot then recipe[1] := recipeIn with ID 0 basically nothing. Not tested. Fine.

Need declarations: FB_Task with VAR_INPUT, VAR_OUTPUT, VAR_IN_OUT, VAR private.

Note: naming conflict — FB named FB_Task, and instance maybe... VAR: rtAdd etc, i : INT, foundIndex, emptyIndex.

Also "status" is WORD; 16#8001 fine.

Write declaration:

```
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task
VAR_INPUT
 addRecipe : BOOL;
 deleteRecipe : BOOL;
 modifyRecipe : BOOL;
 queryRecipe : BOOL;
 recipeIn : ST_Recipe;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
 recipeAdded : BOOL;
 recipeDeleted : BOOL;
 recipeModified : BOOL;
 recipeQueryResult : ST_Recipe;
 error : BOOL;
 status : WORD;
END_VAR
VAR_IN_OUT
 recipe : ARRAY[1..10] OF ST_Recipe;
END_VAR
VAR
 rtAdd : BOOL;
 rtDel : BOOL;
 rtMod : BOOL;
 rtQuery : BOOL;
 i : INT;
 foundIndex : INT;
 emptyIndex : INT;
END_VAR
```

